// Test: bugfixes/ssr_reclaim_no_live_pointer_corruption
// Grammar: while_statement, variable_declaration, assignment, binary_expression
// Semantic: tracking CMP-SSR-RECLAIM-FREES-LIVE-POINTER
//
// Guards the cross-iter live-pointer corruption that the 0.30.373/0.30.374
// `string_builder_reclaim` placement introduced. Shape:
//
//     string head = json.get(j, "0")       // initial head allocation
//     while head != ""
//         acc = acc + "[" + head + "]"     // chained-RHS rewrite fires
//         i = i + 1
//         head = json.get(j, i.toString()) // outer-scope head reassign
//     return acc
//
// The 0.30.374 emission appended `string_builder_reclaim(__sb, mark)` at
// the end of the body. Reclaim sets HEAP_PTR back to the post-builder
// baseline, but the newly-allocated `head` (from `head = json.get(...)`)
// lives ABOVE that baseline. Next iter's condition reads `head` — bytes
// already overwritten by some intervening allocation. Symptom on the
// dashboard was `String read out of bounds: ptr=239468,
// len=1668183366 (= 0x636F643E = ASCII '>doc')`.
//
// Fix: roll back the reclaim emission. The chained-RHS rewrite still
// runs (turns O(n²) accumulator into O(n)); the conditional-helper
// leak is bounded per render and json.get's parse-tree cache (0.30.369)
// keeps it from dominating.
//
// Expected output:
//   9
//   [a][b][c]

start:
	string itemsJson = "[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]"
	string acc = ""
	integer i = 0
	string head = json.get(itemsJson, "0")
	while head != ""
		acc = acc + "[" + head + "]"
		i = i + 1
		head = json.get(itemsJson, i.toString())
	printl(acc.length().toString())
	printl(acc)
